From 4b85ae769c2201935fdafe50bed64fddf41a1edd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:37:34 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 071/101] render: shadows, light cookies, tube and directional
 lights

WE's shadow pass and the rest of its generated lighting (decoded from wallpaper64.exe 2.8.485):
- Lights: castshadow (flags bit 0), usecookie (bit 1) and `cookie` (default cookie/flashlight1,
  GH 0x140282140), `controlpoint` (a tube's far end), lightsourcesize; ltube and ldirectional
  (GH 0x140283df0's table). Models: castshadow.
- The shadow atlas is a depth texture sampled by comparison, 2 x 2 until a light casts a shadow,
  then a 256 px tile per projection (medium quality, GH 0x140282540); it was a scene-sized RGBA8
  target nothing drew. A spot's projection is its outer cone along its x axis; a point light's six
  cube faces share a tile in 2 x 3, as common_pbr_2.h's CalculateProjectedCoordsPoint reads them
  (near 0.05, far the radius, FUN_140282580).
- The casters (materials/util/shadowcaster.json; shadowcasterfoliage4 / fur4 for foliage4 / fur4,
  the mesh's combos) are drawn into each viewport before the scene; WE draws up to six instances,
  one per viewport (gl_ViewportIndex from the vertex unit). LWE draws a viewport at a time and
  drops that write, so the stock casters build on any GL. A polygon offset against acne (inferred).
- PerformLighting_V1 (GH 0x140197e20): the spot cookie and shadow lookups, the point light's cube
  lookup, the tube loop (PointSegmentDelta) and the directional lights; the calls follow the
  common_pbr_2.h the assets ship (2.8.42's or 2.8.485's signatures). Models get
  LIGHTS_SHADOW_MAPPING / _QUALITY 2, LIGHTS_COOKIE and LIGHTS_DIRECTIONAL from the scene's lights,
  and the cookie where they sample _alias_lightCookie.
- texSample2DCompare returns a vec4 (the header reads .r).

Not done: WE's light clusters, the directional cascades, the 2.8.485 PCSS terms, the
lightconfig key.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-coverage.md (F1 shadows and light cookies)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
